      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.668,
            0.065,
            0.834,
            0.081
          ],
          "content": "Perimeter and Area"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.12,
            0.555,
            0.188
          ],
          "content": "Use your understanding from previous grades to calculate the area of any closed figure using grid paper and —"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.192,
            0.553,
            0.237
          ],
          "content": "1. Find the area of blue triangle BAD."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.243,
            0.552,
            0.265
          ],
          "content": "2. Find the area of red triangle ABE."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.282,
            0.535,
            0.435
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_14_image_4.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.562,
            0.118,
            0.834,
            0.309
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_14_image_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.357,
            0.313,
            0.519,
            0.401
          ],
          "content": "Both the red and blue triangles have the same area but they look very different."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.144,
            0.447,
            0.587,
            0.468
          ],
          "content": "Area of rectangle ABCD ="
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.143,
            0.47,
            0.825,
            0.492
          ],
          "content": "So, the area of triangle BAD is half of the area of the rectangle ABCD."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.26,
            0.497,
            0.681,
            0.715
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_14_image_9.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.297,
            0.653,
            0.401,
            0.701
          ],
          "content": "What about triangle ABE?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.728,
            0.825,
            0.808
          ],
          "content": "Area of triangle ABE = Area of triangle AEF + Area of triangle BEF. Here, the area of triangle AEF = half of the area of rectangle AFED. Similarly, the area of triangle BEF = half of the area of rectangle BFEC."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.814,
            0.834,
            0.861
          ],
          "content": "Thus, the area of triangle ABE = half of the area of rectangle AFED +half of the area of rectangle BFEC"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.885,
            0.942,
